//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Guilds
// Switch and size of the battle.
//   Event is on: 1 turns the event on, 0 off.
//   Guilds needed: Fewest guilds (with enough players) needed for the battle to start; with fewer the event is cancelled.
//   Guilds allowed: Most guilds that fight; the ones that came last are sent out.
//   Players per guild, at least: Fewest players a guild needs inside to take part; smaller guilds are sent out.
//   Players per guild, at most: Most players of one guild that can enter.
//   Take the points away when the player dies: 1 makes a player lose all his points when he dies (they are also taken away from his guild).
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [0~1]      [1~10]       [2~10]       [1~30]           [1~30]           [0~1]
//  Enabled    MinGuilds    MaxGuilds    MinGuildUsers    MaxGuildUsers    RemovePointsWhenDie
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
0
    1          2            10           1                10               1
end

//----------------------------------------------------------
// Timing
// The times of one battle.
//   Waiting room (seconds): Seconds in the waiting area before the battle starts.
//   Battle (minutes): Minutes the battle lasts.
//   Closing (seconds): Seconds after the battle before everyone is moved out.
//----------------------------------------------------------
//  WaitTime    BattleTime    FinishTime
//----------------------------------------------------------
1
    10          3             10
end

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Who Can Enter
// What a player needs to enter the waiting area. The player must have a guild.
//   Required item: Item category of the item that is taken when entering. * asks for no item.
//   Required item index: Item index of the item that is taken when entering. * asks for no item.
//   Item level: Level of the item asked for.
//   How many: How many of that item are taken from each player.
//   Every player pays it: Sent to the client window; the server does not check it (unverified).
//   Highest PK level allowed: Not used by the server for this event (unverified).
//   Break up the party on entry: 1 removes the player from his party when he enters.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [*/0~15]    [*/0~511]    [0~15]       [0~99]       [Number]        [0~6]         [Number]
//  ItemType    ItemIndex    ItemLevel    ItemCount    ItemAllUsers    MaxPKLevel    DisolveParty
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2
    12          15           0            1            1               3             1
end

//--------------------------------------------------------------
// Battle Zones
// Areas of the battle (a rectangle on a map). Add several Respawn rows: each guild is given a different one at random.
//   Zone: 0 Waiting Area | 1 Battle Area | 2 Respawn Area | 3 End Area
//   Map: Map of the area.
//   Left side: Left side of the area.
//   Top side: Top side of the area.
//   Right side: Right side of the area.
//   Bottom side: Bottom side of the area.
//--------------------------------------------------------------
//  [0~3]    [0~199]    [0~254]    [0~254]    [0~254]    [0~254]
//  Zone     Map        X1         Y1         X2         Y2
//--------------------------------------------------------------
3
    0        0          140        123        148        132        //Waiting Area
    1        0          140        123        148        132        //Battle Area
    2        0          140        123        148        132        //Respawn Area [1]
    2        0          140        123        148        132        //Respawn Area [2]
    2        0          140        123        148        132        //Respawn Area [3]
    2        0          140        123        148        132        //Respawn Area [4]
    2        0          140        123        148        132        //Respawn Area [5]
    2        0          140        123        148        132        //Respawn Area [6]
    2        0          140        123        148        132        //Respawn Area [7]
    2        0          140        123        148        132        //Respawn Area [8]
    3        2          220        40         225        45         //End Area
end

//----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Schedule
// When the event opens. The second is not used: it starts on the minute.
//   Year: The year when the event opens. * means every year.
//   Month: The month when the event opens. * means every month.
//   Day: The day of the month when the event opens. * means every day of the month.
//   Day of the week: -1 Every day | 1 Sunday | 2 Monday | 3 Tuesday | 4 Wednesday | 5 Thursday | 6 Friday | 7 Saturday
//   Hour: The hour when the event opens. * means every hour.
//   Minute: The minute when the event opens. * means every minute.
//   Second: The second when the event opens. * means every second.
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [*/1970~9999]    [*/1~12]    [*/1~31]    [*/1~7]      [*/0~23]    [*/0~59]    [*/0~59]
//  Year             Month       Day         DayOfWeek    Hour        Minute      Second
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4
    *                *           *           *            15          0           0           //
end

//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Winner Guild Reward
// Prize for every player of the winning guild (the guild with the most points).
//   WCoin C: WCoin C given to each player of the winning guild. 0 gives none.
//   WCoin P: WCoin P given to each player of the winning guild. 0 gives none.
//   Goblin Points: Goblin Points given to each player of the winning guild. 0 gives none.
//   Ruud: Ruud given to each player of the winning guild. 0 gives none.
//   Item Bag: Item bag dropped for each player of the winning guild. * gives none.
//   Buff: Effect (Effect.txt) given as a buff. * or 0 gives none.
//   Buff time (minutes): Minutes the buff lasts (the server multiplies it by 60, so the value is in minutes, not seconds).
//   Buff value 1: First power value of the buff (see the effect).
//   Buff value 2: Second power value of the buff (see the effect).
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [Number]    [Number]    [Number]    [Number]    [Number]
//  WC               WP               GP               Ruuds            ItemBag     Buff        BuffTime    Val1        Val2
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5
    9                0                0                0                *           *           0           0           0
end

//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Guild Ranking Rewards
// Prizes for the other guilds by their position. The winner uses the part above, so start at position 2. Every player of the guild gets it.
//   Position: Position of the guild in the ranking (2 is second place).
//   WCoin C: WCoin C given to each player of that guild. 0 gives none.
//   WCoin P: WCoin P given to each player of that guild. 0 gives none.
//   Goblin Points: Goblin Points given to each player of that guild. 0 gives none.
//   Ruud: Ruud given to each player of that guild. 0 gives none.
//   Item Bag: Item bag dropped for each player of that guild. * gives none.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [1~100]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [Number]
//  Top        WC               WP               GP               Ruuds            ItemBag
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6
    2          8                0                0                0                *
end


//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Player Ranking Rewards
// Prizes for the players with the most points (individual ranking).
//   Position: Position of the player in the ranking (1 is the best player).
//   WCoin C: WCoin C given to that player. 0 gives none.
//   WCoin P: WCoin P given to that player. 0 gives none.
//   Goblin Points: Goblin Points given to that player. 0 gives none.
//   Ruud: Ruud given to that player. 0 gives none.
//   Item Bag: Item bag dropped for that player. * gives none.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [1~100]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [Number]
//  Top        WC               WP               GP               Ruuds            ItemBag
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7
    1          8                0                0                0                *
    2          6                0                0                0                *
    3          4                0                0                0                *
end


//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//	Kill Points
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//----------------------------------------------------------
// Kill Points
// Points a kill gives, by the rank of the player killed in his guild.
//   Killed player's rank: 1 Guild Master | 2 Assistant Guild Master | 3 Battle Master | 4 Member
//   Points: Points the killer gets for killing a player of that rank.
//----------------------------------------------------------
//  Range    Points
//----------------------------------------------------------
8
    1        10
    2        8
    3        8
    4        5
end